{
  "$schema": "./schema/anomaly.schema.json",
  "design_notes": [
    "Cards, trigger texts and responses are those of table 6.8. \"Every 3–5 votes\" is draw.min_votes_between 3 and max_votes_between 5.",
    "The design gives no draw weight for any card. base_weight and every weight_mult in this file are chosen by the data author (game values, to be tuned with playtests).",
    "How the weights are meant to be used: weight = base_weight × the weight_mult of every trigger that holds. A trigger without weight_mult is a gate: the card can be drawn only while it holds (test_revealed_flaw, test_skipped, payload_contract, science_payload, and the part_rule of Contamination in Clean Room). The kinds random and rare only describe the card. Core must confirm or replace this rule.",
    "A part_rule trigger holds when a chosen part has an anomaly_weight rule for the card. The multiplier applies once, however many parts carry the rule. Cards tied to one place or one kind of hardware have a low base weight and a high multiplier (range_conflict, helium_shortage, lightning_season), so they are rare without the part.",
    "Response effects carry a number only where the design prints one: +$4 M, +12 days, −10% budget, +2% Δv, −5 days, 5 days, +3 days, +$1 M and +2 days, 3 days, +$1 M. The rest (\"+$\", \"+days\", \"reliability −\", \"+$ overtime\", \"+mass\", \"science penalty\", \"less Δv margin\", \"scrub\") have no amount in the design and are flags.",
    "Money is stored as an addition to cost_M and days as an addition to schedule_days.",
    "Appendix A shows the delay of Supplier Delay as the default and the payment as the way out; the effects therefore sit on the responses, not on the card.",
    "Launch sites refer to \"tropical storm\" and \"fog\" cards that do not exist in this table; launch_site.json maps them to weather_front."
  ],
  "draw": {
    "min_votes_between": 3,
    "max_votes_between": 5
  },
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "id": "supplier_delay",
      "name_key": "anomaly.supplier_delay.name",
      "trigger_key": "anomaly.supplier_delay.trigger",
      "base_weight": 1,
      "triggers": [
        {
          "kind": "part_rule",
          "weight_mult": 2
        }
      ],
      "responses": [
        {
          "id": "pay_to_expedite",
          "text_key": "anomaly.supplier_delay.response.pay_to_expedite",
          "effects": [
            {
              "target": "cost_M",
              "op": "add",
              "value": 4,
              "scope": "mission"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "accept_delay",
          "text_key": "anomaly.supplier_delay.response.accept_delay",
          "effects": [
            {
              "target": "schedule_days",
              "op": "add",
              "value": 12,
              "scope": "mission"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "switch_part",
          "text_key": "anomaly.supplier_delay.response.switch_part",
          "action": "swap_part"
        }
      ],
      "design_notes": [
        "The design does not say what the alternative part costs or whether the swap is a free re-vote."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "budget_cut",
      "name_key": "anomaly.budget_cut.name",
